  <h2>🎮 Setting Up the Discord Agent Bot</h2>
  <p>
    The Discord bot leverages Discord Slash Commands and channel threads for multi-project development:
  </p>

  <ol>
    <li>Create an application in the <a href="https://discord.com/developers/applications" target="_blank" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">Discord Developer Portal</a>.</li>
    <li>Under <strong>Bot</strong>, copy your <strong>Bot Token</strong> and enable <strong>Message Content Intent</strong>.</li>
    <li>Copy your personal numeric <strong>Discord User ID</strong> (Enable Developer Mode in Discord ➔ Right-click your avatar ➔ Copy User ID).</li>
    <li>In OMV WebGUI ➔ <strong>Services ➔ Agent Station ➔ Chat & Messenger</strong>:
      <ul>
        <li>Paste your <strong>Discord Bot Token</strong> and <strong>Discord Allowed User ID</strong>.</li>
        <li>Click <strong>Save</strong> and <strong>Apply</strong>.</li>
      </ul>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h3>🧵 Thread & Channel Context Binding</h3>
  <p>
    Inside any Discord channel or thread, use <code>/bind &lt;project-name&gt;</code> to lock that channel to a specific repository. Once bound, all subsequent <code>/task</code>, <code>/diff</code>, <code>/push</code>, and <code>/pull</code> commands automatically execute against that project workspace.
  </p>

  <h2>🔒 Setting Up the Signal Messenger Bot</h2>
  <p>
    The Signal bot uses a local <code>signal-cli-rest-api</code> container for end-to-end encrypted messaging with zero third-party cloud data retention:
  </p>

  <ol>
    <li>Register or link a dedicated Signal phone number for your OMV server using <code>signal-cli</code>.</li>
    <li>In OMV WebGUI ➔ <strong>Services ➔ Agent Station ➔ Chat & Messenger</strong>:
      <ul>
        <li>Enter your <strong>Signal Phone Number</strong> (e.g. <code>+1234567890</code>).</li>
        <li>Enter your <strong>Signal Allowed Number</strong> for authorized commands.</li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li>Save and apply configuration in OMV.</li>
  </ol>

  <h3>💬 Conversational Natural Language Mode</h3>
  <p>
    On Signal and Telegram private chats, sending any message without a slash prefix automatically queries the <code>coder-smart</code> AI router, giving you an instant AI coding companion right inside your private messages.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
